# The front of a loop that stores a number into a list asked for the one storage that would HOLD the number. A whole number laid into a list of doubles, a fraction laid into a list of any values failed it, and the
# closed, rare copy ran: 8,270 and 6,990 instructions a call of 256 stores, plain Bun 1,560. Every plain writable storage TAKES a number: boxed into int32s (an int32 alone) and into any values, raw into doubles.
# The walk: the front asks for any of them; the store is one operation that goes by the kind found. The code generator: the turns are laid out in a row once for boxed storage and once for doubles, the kind asked in
# front of them, as for lists that are read and for views; the rest of fewer turns asks in place. All five roads: 1,880. A list of int32s that is to take fractions is converted in front, as before.
# `shift` reads its list by key: it goes on asking for int32 storage, which types the read.
# f1 = fill, f2 = halve, f3 = shift
# RUN: compile LoopsLaidOutForOneKindOfStorage mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic LoopsLaidOutForOneKindOfStorage 4
# RUN(FILL): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# FILL-NOT: arrayStorage=Contiguous
# FILL: [isWritable, admitsInt32Storage]
# FILL: [goesByKindOfStorage]
# RUN(HALVE): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# HALVE: ConvertToDoubleStorage
# HALVE-NOT: arrayStorage=Double
# HALVE: [isWritable]
# HALVE: [goesByKindOfStorage]
# RUN(SHIFT): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# SHIFT: arrayStorage=Int32 [isWritable]
# SHIFT: PutContiguousIndex
# SHIFT-NOT: [goesByKindOfStorage]
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
